    "causal_summary": "Notion formulas support `let()` / `lets()` to bind named intermediate values in a per-row child scope (`let(person, \"Alan\", \"Hello, \" + person + \"!\")` = `\"Hello, Alan!\"`); the fork's native engine (`ComputedField.ts` over the `SafeEval.ts` sandbox) has no binding construct, so long formulas duplicate sub-expressions",
